WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.590
CHANGYANG LINGHU: My
name is Changyang Linghu.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.690
I am developing new
technologies for detecting

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.870
the symphony of cellular
activities in the brain.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.400
The brain uses many
different kinds

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.785
of simultaneously interacting
signals to function.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.810
All of the signals
working together

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:22.760
in harmony in the healthy brain.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.610
To understand this harmony, we
need to measure these signals

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.810
at the same time.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:30.320
Up to now, most scientists can
only image one or two signals

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.290
at a time, because the number
of signal reporters that

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.660
can be used together is
limited to the number

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.700
of available colors
on the microscope.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.090
We have just developed
a new technology

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.180
that allows us to record
multiple signals in real time

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.580
regardless of the
color of reporters.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.675
We call it Signaling Reporter
Islands, or SiRIs, for short.

00:00:50.675 --> 00:00:54.320
It works by spatially
separating the signal reporters

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:57.020
into small islands
throughout the cell.

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.140
First, we engineer signal
reporters to self-assemble

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.150
into SiRI islands in the cell.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.790
Next, we record individual
cellular signals

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.930
by capturing the light emitted
from individual SiRI islands.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.840
Then we fix the cells and
perform immune staining

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.180
to identify distinct
tags bound to each

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.100
of the different reporters.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.620
Finally, we attributed
the light emissions

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.690
to the corresponding
cellular signals

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.330
according to the
immunostain results.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:26.032
We measured five signals
together in the first paper,

00:01:26.032 --> 00:01:27.740
but we are working to
increase the number

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.750
to 10s of individual signals.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.180
We're hoping that by
measuring multiple aspects

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.100
of the cellular
symphony in parallel,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.870
we can pinpoint the
exact differences

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.760
between healthy
and diseased brains

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.220
and provide insights
into new treatments.

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.670
[MUSIC PLAYING]

